{
  "slug": "keynot",
  "name": "Keynot",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "A Claude Code skill that turns any prompt into a polished, self-contained HTML slide deck — keyboard navigation, swipe, fullscreen, animated reveals, brand-accurate design. Single file. Opens anywhere. No runtime dependencies.\n\nBuilt for the moment you need to present something and you don't want to open PowerPoint.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `keynot` (Create polished, self-contained HTML slide presentations — no PowerPoint or Keynote needed).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install keynot@claude-community` from `shawnzam/keynot`.\n\nSomeone asks you to \"put together a few slides\" and your hand drifts to the PowerPoint icon out of pure muscle memory. Then come the next twenty minutes of fighting a template you didn't pick, nudging a text box three pixels to the left, and discovering that your brand colors aren't in the theme. None of that is the presentation.…",
  "compatibility": [
